Package: ukbcareer
Title: Lifetime Work-History Variables for UK Biobank
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Jie", family = "Zhang",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "changchieh1998@163.com")
Author: Jie Zhang [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Jie Zhang <changchieh1998@163.com>
Description: Turns the UK Biobank lifetime work history (Category 130:
    every job and every break, with hours, shift work and ten workplace
    exposures) into analysis-ready, one-row-per-person variables: when and how
    the career ended, working years, cumulative exposures, shift work and long
    hours, occupational status (CAMSIS), occupational mobility and data
    quality flags. Also provides annual state sequences for sequence analysis,
    a one-page visual report of any participant's career, and, with the
    optional pretrained model, a career representation and career types
    re-derived on the user's own sample. Definitions follow the accompanying
    paper, so results are comparable across studies. The package derives
    exposures only; it contains no individual-level data.
